- **`workflows/performance-problem.sm.yaml` + `skills/performance-problem/SKILL.md`**
  — novel to AIECP. performance-problem is the workflow for
  "it's slow" / latency / throughput complaints — distinct from
  bug-report (functional failure) because the code produces correct
  output, just too slowly. Unique structural features: (1) requires
  an `environment_fingerprint_ref` at the baseline stage (performance
  is environment-sensitive — same code, different hardware,
  different result); (2) the `verify-improvement` state requires
  BOTH a performance check AND a functional regression check (a
  speedup that breaks tests is not an improvement); (3) the
  `regression-protect` state writes a `known-failure` memory entry
  for a PERFORMANCE regression (not a functional one), so future
  code that reintroduces the slow pattern fires the `regression`
  workflow. The profiler-commands-per-language reference (Node
  --prof, Python cProfile, Go pprof, Swift Instruments) is curated
  from general performance-engineering practice, no single upstream
  source. No upstream code or prose was adapted or copied.

